{"path":"numeric/midpoint","title":"std::midpoint","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>midpoint","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/numeric/midpoint","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"Computes the midpoint of the integers, floating-points, or pointers a and b.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/numeric\">&lt;numeric&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> T midpoint<span class=\"br0\">(</span> T a, T b <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> T<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> midpoint<span class=\"br0\">(</span> T<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> a, T<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> b <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Computes the midpoint of the integers, floating-points, or pointers <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">a</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">b</span></code>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> This overload participates in overload resolution only if <code>T</code> is an arithmetic type other than <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span></span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> This overload participates in overload resolution only if <code>T</code> is an object type. Use of this overload is ill-formed if <code>T</code> is an <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/type#Incomplete_type\">incomplete type</a>.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters </h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> a, b\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> integers, floating-points, or pointer values\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Half the sum of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">a</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">b</span></code>. No overflow occurs. If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">a</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">b</span></code> have integer type and the sum is odd, the result is rounded towards <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">a</span></code>. If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">a</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">b</span></code> have floating-point type, at most one inexact operation occurs.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">a</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">b</span></code> point to, respectively, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x<span class=\"br0\">[</span>i<span class=\"br0\">]</span></span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x<span class=\"br0\">[</span>j<span class=\"br0\">]</span></span></code> of the same array object <code>x</code> (for the purpose of <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/operator_arithmetic#Additive_operators\">pointer arithmetic</a>), returns a pointer to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x<span class=\"br0\">[</span>i <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>j <span class=\"sy2\">-</span> i<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span></span></code> (or, equivalently <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x<span class=\"br0\">[</span>std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">midpoint</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>i, j<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span></span></code>) where the division rounds towards zero. If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">a</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">b</span></code> do not point to elements of the same array object, the behavior is undefined.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions </h3>\n<p>Throws no exceptions.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Overload <span class=\"t-v\">(2)</span> can be simply implemented as <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">return</span> a <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>b <span class=\"sy2\">-</span> a<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code> on common platforms. However, such implementation is not guaranteed to be portable, because there may be some platforms where creating an array with number of elements greater than <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/climits\">PTRDIFF_MAX</a></span> is possible, and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">b <span class=\"sy2\">-</span> a</span></code> may result in undefined behavior even if both <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">b</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">a</span></code> point to elements in the same array.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable ftm-begin ftm-has-value\">\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/feature_test\">Feature-test</a> macro</th>\n<th><abbr>Value</abbr></th>\n<th><abbr>Std</abbr></th>\n<th>Feature\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/feature_test#cpp_lib_interpolate\"><code>__cpp_lib_interpolate</code></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/compiler_support/20#cpp_lib_interpolate_201902L\"><code>201902L</code></a></td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark\">(C++20)</span></td>\n<td><span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/lerp\">std::lerp</a></span>, <code>std::midpoint</code>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cstdint&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;limits&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;numeric&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/integer\"><span class=\"kw129\">std::<span class=\"me2\">uint32_t</span></span></a> a <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits\"><span class=\"kw351\">std::<span class=\"me2\">numeric_limits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/integer\"><span class=\"kw129\">std::<span class=\"me2\">uint32_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">max</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/integer\"><span class=\"kw129\">std::<span class=\"me2\">uint32_t</span></span></a> b <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits\"><span class=\"kw351\">std::<span class=\"me2\">numeric_limits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/integer\"><span class=\"kw129\">std::<span class=\"me2\">uint32_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">max</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span> <span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"a: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> a <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"b: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> b <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Incorrect (overflow and wrapping): \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>a <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> b<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <span class=\"nu0\">2</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Correct: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">midpoint</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>a, b<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span><span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> on_pointers <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span> i, <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> j<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> text <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"0123456789\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> p <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> text <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> i<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> q <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> text <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> j<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"std::midpoint('\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>p <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"', '\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>q <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"'): '\"</span>\n                  <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">midpoint</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>p, q<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    on_pointers<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">4</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    on_pointers<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">5</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    on_pointers<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">5</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    on_pointers<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">6</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>a: 4294967295\nb: 4294967293\nIncorrect (overflow and wrapping): 2147483646\nCorrect: 4294967294\n&nbsp;\nstd::midpoint('2', '4'): '3'\nstd::midpoint('2', '5'): '3'\nstd::midpoint('5', '2'): '4'\nstd::midpoint('2', '6'): '4'</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"References\">References</h3>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c++23\">\n<ul><li> C++23 standard (ISO/IEC 14882:2024): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 27.10.16 Midpoint [numeric.ops.midpoint] \n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c++20\">\n<ul><li> C++20 standard (ISO/IEC 14882:2020): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 25.10.15 Midpoint [numeric.ops.midpoint] \n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/lerp\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>lerp</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  linear interpolation function <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"References","id":"References"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics library"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::midpoint","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++20. Computes the midpoint of the integers, floating-points, or pointers a and b."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"a, b"},{"label":"Return value","note":"Half the sum of a and b. No overflow occurs. If a and b have integer type and the sum is odd, the result is rounded towards a."},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"Throws no exceptions."},{"label":"Notes","note":"Overload (2) can be simply implemented as return a + (b - a) / 2; on common platforms."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"lerp","note":"linear interpolation function"}]}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":446,"codeBlockCount":2}
